  "summary": "I have 20 years of experience as a professional librarian working in higher education, and nearly 10 years of experience in data analysis and software development, including full-stack development with Python, Ruby, Go, SQL, and Javascript. In my current role, I build and maintain open-source applications, including our university's institutional repository (a Ruby on Rails application); and I design and implement cloud-based solutions for a variety of needs across the institution. \n\nI thrive in collaborative environments with a user-focused mission. I regularly apply Agile methods to the execution of complex projects, and I am a skilled communicator, able to translate project requirements and outcomes for a wide variety of stakeholders.\n\nI also have deep experience in teaching. I have taught library research methods to students from the undergraduate to the doctoral level, and I currently support computational literacy by offering workshops and consultations on software development and data analysis for faculty, staff, and students.",
